cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Analysis code for "Transporter abundance is preserved while transport fails:
  re-examining EAAT2/SLC1A2 in the Alzheimer brain through the lens of estimand
  specification"
message: >-
  If you use this code or the extraction matrix, please cite the accompanying
  manuscript.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alper
    family-names: Karagöl
    email: akaragol@mit.edu
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0001-7864-0732'
    affiliation: Istanbul University Istanbul Medical Faculty, Istanbul, Turkey
  - given-names: Taner
    family-names: Karagöl
    email: karagolt@mit.edu
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0005-1011-7661'
    affiliation: Istanbul University Istanbul Medical Faculty, Istanbul, Turkey
abstract: >-
  Reproducible analysis code, extraction matrix and document sources for a
  quantitative evidence synthesis of post-mortem EAAT2/SLC1A2 measurements in
  Alzheimer's disease. Regenerates every statistic and figure reported in the
  manuscript and supplementary material from fixed random seeds.
keywords:
  - EAAT2
  - SLC1A2
  - GLT-1
  - Alzheimer's disease
  - astrocyte
  - glutamate transport
  - evidence synthesis
  - reproducible research
